[
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm trying to formalize a well-known determinization construction for Büchi automata:<br>\n<a href=\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/21948\">https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/21948</a><br>\nThis construction uses a tree data type in which each node can have a variable number of kids (including zero).  So I end up with a definition like the following:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SafraTree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">node</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">stable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">kids</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">SafraTree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SafraTree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>To reason about <code>SafraTree</code>, I would like to use this library:<br>\n<a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"579630\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/579630-Project-announcements/topic/Leanduction.3A.20Nested.20inductive.20types.20made.20simple/with/614959257\">#Project announcements &gt; Leanduction: Nested inductive types made simple</a> <br>\nWhat is the best method to introduce this dependency in CSLib?</p>\n<p>If anyone has a clever idea for avoiding nested inductive types, I would like to hear about it, too.</p>",
        "id": 615516827,
        "sender_full_name": "Ching-Tsun Chou",
        "timestamp": 1786321335
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The way I solve this right now is to write sparse recursor(s) by hand, which is sad boilerplate every time...</p>\n<p>I'd love to have a standard command for this, as this problem will appear repeatedly in CSLib (esp. as we add more languages).</p>\n<p>From a cursory look, this doesn't look ready to be a CSLib dep: I don't see CI/CD for keeping in line with the last version of Lean, for example. If there are no other plans anywhere, we could consider 'incubating' something like this in CSLib until it becomes mature/interesting enough to be upstreamed.<br>\nTo do this, the best would be that (a) the author (<span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"432410\">@Arthur Adjedj</span>) is interested and (b) we have somebody willing to review the code.</p>",
        "id": 615552698,
        "sender_full_name": "Fabrizio Montesi",
        "timestamp": 1786344202
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'd add here a requirement about only adding dependencies supported by the new nightly testing setup at <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/downstream-lean4\">https://github.com/leanprover/downstream-lean4</a>.</p>",
        "id": 615556810,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1786345578
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I would be happy to add whichever CI/CD might be relevant/useful (I have only relied on the default <code>lean-action</code> for now). Similarly, while the code is documented, I can spend some time documenting it more, and providing guidance to whoever would be willing to review it <span aria-label=\"slight smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f642\" role=\"img\" title=\"slight smile\">:slight_smile:</span> <br>\nI do not really understand why every dependency of Mathlib (and transitively, CSLib) gets upstreamed to leanprover-community rather than stay in their respective repository, not that would mind this happening in practice.</p>",
        "id": 615557015,
        "sender_full_name": "Arthur Adjedj",
        "timestamp": 1786345641
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>One reason for this is that it automatically gives the right people permissions to bump all those dependencies to new Lean versions, or even nightlies</p>",
        "id": 615560079,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Ullrich",
        "timestamp": 1786346767
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Perhaps I can get away with not using nested inductive types in this case by defining <code>SafraTree</code> in a different way:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SafraTree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">node</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">stable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">knum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">kmap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">knum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SafraTree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SafraTree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I just tested and it seems that Lean lets me do induction on this version of <code>SafraTree</code>.  The list of kids can be obtained using <code>List.ofFn</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">kids</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SafraTree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">SafraTree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">node</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">kmap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofFn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">kmap</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Going the other direction is also easy.</p>",
        "id": 615680510,
        "sender_full_name": "Ching-Tsun Chou",
        "timestamp": 1786383745
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I wonder if it would be better to have</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">node</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">value</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">children</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Tree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(or the <code>Fin</code> version) and recover that variant with <code>α</code> as an appropriate structure</p>",
        "id": 615685518,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1786384994
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That's a good idea.  Thanks!</p>",
        "id": 615726891,
        "sender_full_name": "Ching-Tsun Chou",
        "timestamp": 1786400901
    },
